Show the KMS that seals the keys of the SSE-S3 and SSE-KMS objects (the builtin
KMS of NEXO_KMS_SECRET_KEY or an external KES server) and manage its keys: a
key created here is usable as SSE-KMS key ("nexoctl encrypt set sse-kms KEY",
"nexoctl cp --enc-kms").

Usage:
  nexoctl admin kms [flags]
  nexoctl admin kms [command]

Available Commands:
  key         Create and list the keys of the KMS
  status      Show the state of the KMS

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for kms

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin kms [command] --help" for more information about a command.
